.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-aep-verify - Verify the ECDSA signature of a signed AEP receipt


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel aep verify  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Verify the ECDSA signature of a signed AEP receipt (v1 or v2).

.PP
The verifying public key is resolved in this order:
  --cert     take the public key from an X.509 certificate
  --pubkey   a PKIX/SPKI PEM public key
  (default)            this node's local identity key

.PP
The key's fingerprint is compared to the receipt's public_key_fingerprint
before the signature is checked, so a receipt signed by a different node is
reported distinctly from a genuinely invalid signature.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--cert\fP=""
	Path to an X.509 certificate (PEM) whose public key verifies the receipt

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for verify

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Emit a machine-readable JSON result

.PP
\fB--pubkey\fP=""
	Path to a PKIX/SPKI PEM public key to verify against

.PP
\fB--show-canonical\fP[=false]
	Print the exact canonical bytes that were signed to stderr


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--node-dir\fP=""
	Override the node config directory (citadel.yaml + services/), bypassing $HOME/ConfigDir resolution. Also settable via CITADEL_NODE_DIR. Scope: manifest/services resolution only -- does NOT redirect network state, the module lockfile, or nodevault.

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel-aep(1)\fP
